{"name":"Hope Chest","hex":"#875942","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hope chest","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A box containing items, especially clothing, table linens, towels, bed linens, and quilts, typically stored by unmarried young women in anticipation of future married life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hope_chest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hope chest","blocks":[{"text":"A hope chest, also called dowry chest, cedar chest, trousseau chest, or glory box, is a piece of furniture once commonly used by unmarried young women to collect items, such as clothing and household linen, in anticipation of married life."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Walnut_hope_chest_%281570_-_1600%2C_in_Northern_Italy%29._Nymph._-_Budapest_Museum_of_Applied_Arts.JPG/330px-Walnut_hope_chest_%281570_-_1600%2C_in_Northern_Italy%29._Nymph._-_Budapest_Museum_of_Applied_Arts.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hope_chest"},{"title":"Hope","blocks":[{"text":"Hope is an optimistic state of mind that is based on an expectation of desirable outcomes with respect to events and circumstances in one's own life, or the world at large. As a verb, Merriam-Webster defines hope as \"to expect with confidence\" or \"to cherish a desire with anticipation\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Hopeful.jpg/330px-Hopeful.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hope"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Walnut_hope_chest_%281570_-_1600%2C_in_Northern_Italy%29._Nymph._-_Budapest_Museum_of_Applied_Arts.JPG/500px-Walnut_hope_chest_%281570_-_1600%2C_in_Northern_Italy%29._Nymph._-_Budapest_Museum_of_Applied_Arts.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.w